(* The working loop, as a grammar.

   Source for docs/images/working-loop.svg. Rendered with
   https://ys-math.github.io/syntax-diagram-generator/ — paste this file in,
   choose EBNF (ISO/IEC 14977), set Fit to Wrap, and export the SVG.

   One rule on purpose: the generator draws one diagram per rule, and a sitting
   in this repo is one picture, not eight. The named sub-steps live in the boxes
   rather than in rules of their own.

   Quoted terminals are slash commands and are checked — scripts/test_agent_docs.py
   fails if this file names a command that .claude/commands/ does not have. The
   check runs one way only: a command may exist without appearing here.
   /delete-topic is deliberately absent, being an exit rather than a step.

   Special sequences (? … ?) are the parts that are not a command: writing,
   fixing, proving. They are where most of the time actually goes. *)

session =
    { "/new-topic"
    | ? write a chapter ? , [ "/label" ]
    | "/review-notes" , [ "/issues" ] , { ? fix a finding ? }
    | "/formalize" , { ? replace a sorry ? }
    | ? edit the machinery ? , [ "/audit" ]
    } ,
    "/git" , [ "/watch-ci" ] , [ "/git-merge" ] ;
